  "student_passage": "There (1) ____ three long tables in the art room last Friday. We put three old (2) ____ under them to keep the floor clear. It was the first meeting of (3) ____ kite club, and nobody knew exactly how large a kite should be.\n\nOur teacher showed us how to join the thin sticks. We worked (4) ____ because they could break easily. I (5) ____ a blue bird on a piece of paper, while Ben made a kite with red and white squares. We did not try to fly them that afternoon. The teacher said the next meeting would be the (6) ____ one, and then we could use the school field.\n\nA very (7) ____ student from the class next door came in to help us tidy up. She knew where all the brushes belonged. We thanked her (8) ____ we would not have found the right cupboard without her.\n\nI carried my kite home (9) ____ both hands so that its corners would not touch the pavement. At three o'clock next Friday, we hope (10) ____ some younger pupils prepare their own kites. I will not be an expert by then, but I can show them what I learnt about joining the sticks.",
