  "filled_passage": "There (1) were three long tables in the art room last Friday. We put three old (2) boxes under them to keep the floor clear. It was the first meeting of (3) our kite club, and nobody knew exactly how large a kite should be.\n\nOur teacher showed us how to join the thin sticks. We worked (4) carefully because they could break easily. I (5) painted a blue bird on a piece of paper, while Ben made a kite with red and white squares. We did not try to fly them that afternoon. The teacher said the next meeting would be the (6) second one, and then we could use the school field.\n\nA very (7) friendly student from the class next door came in to help us tidy up. She knew where all the brushes belonged. We thanked her (8) because we would not have found the right cupboard without her.\n\nI carried my kite home (9) with both hands so that its corners would not touch the pavement. At three o'clock next Friday, we hope (10) to help some younger pupils prepare their own kites. I will not be an expert by then, but I can show them what I learnt about joining the sticks.",
